%N A399699 Decimal expansion of the probability that the cycle-following strategy succeeds in the 100 prisoners problem.
%C A399699 This is the probability that a uniformly random permutation of 100 elements has no cycle longer than 50. Each prisoner may open at most 50 drawers.
%H A399699 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/100PrisonersProblem.html">100 Prisoners Problem</a>.
%F A399699 Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*10^(-n-1) = 1 - Sum_{k=51..100} 1/k = 1 - H_100 + H_50 = 21740752665556690246055199895649405434183/69720375229712477164533808935312303556800, where H_n = Sum_{k=1..n} 1/k.
%e A399699 0.31182782068980479675535411730651593406162969725900...
%t A399699 RealDigits[1 - HarmonicNumber[100] + HarmonicNumber[50], 10, 120][[1]]
%t A399699 RealDigits[{1, 1, -1} . HarmonicNumber[{1, 50, 100}], 10, 120][[1]]
%K A399699 nonn,cons,base,new
%O A399699 0,1
%A A399699 _Eric W. Weisstein_, Sep 08 2026
